      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Foreign bodies are a common problem in the daily endoscopic practice. Nevertheless, long objects as toothbrushes, sometimes pose a special problem when trying to remove them from the stomach, due to the difficulty of passing through the hiatus. Endoscopic retrieval of toothbrushes has seldom be reported."},
